<p>In <a href="https://chrismaiorana.com/the-emacs-way-deleting-files/">the last article</a> in the series, we talked about deleting files, which is scary and sad. In this article, I’m happy to change topics into creation territory as we learn how to create directories in the UNIXy way and the Emacs way.</p>
<p>Which way is better? I leave that up to you, but you should know both, because context matters, and there be times when you need one because the other one might not be available.</p>
<p><b>Remember, in your computer everything is a file, even directories are files that point to other files.</b></p>
<p>So let’s get into it.</p>
